# will_backtrack — a will's way back is settled on the area its path needs, and nothing is asked
#
# Lockpicking wants the Test Door, off the yard. The visit opens in the yard and walks out to the
# field; from the field the yard is a place already stood in, so walking to it is not offered and
# going back is. The will's plan therefore begins with a backtrack, settled on the yard ("go back to
# the test yard"), and past the dice the location map asks nothing: the party goes straight back.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm lockpicking,woodcraft --grant-item hairpin --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Field"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Out to the field, by a way not known yet.
strategy succeed
goal move
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Field

# In the field the will plans back through the yard.
observe "Test Yard"
click button
advance 12 180
expect-state will go back to the test yard, the way I know

means woodcraft
click keyword yard
choose 0
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
regions
expect go back to the test yard

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Moved to: Test Yard
expect-verb backtrack
expect-state where Test Yard
quit
